Report what the packet timeline does, and keep a capture whose timestamps stay ahead of the clock.

The timeline held, trimmed and dropped packets without a trace. Each capture now counts corrected timestamps, dropped held packets, short gaps, trimmed frames and timestamps ahead of the clock, and writes one line a minute, and one when it ends, while any of them is not zero. After 100 timestamps more than 2 ms ahead of the clock, anchor to arrival and advance by frame count. Correct drift against arrival only at the start of a batch.

